# The Better Auth adapter's one route (core/packages/providers/auth/better-auth/README.md): public, no
# body. `linkToken` is the token of a link mailed to Mailpit: put it in http-client.private.env.json,
# never here. The GET spends nothing (the confirm step); the POST works once, and a used, expired or
# refused link lands on the same failure page.

### GET /api/auth/magic-link/verify: opens a sign-in link; 303 to /sign-in/confirm?link=<the link>, no session
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/magic-link/verify?token={{linkToken}}&callbackURL=/

### POST /api/auth/magic-link/verify: the confirm page's button; 303 to callbackURL with the session cookie, or 303 to /sign-in/expired?code=auth_link_expired
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/magic-link/verify?token={{linkToken}}&callbackURL=/
Origin: {{appOrigin}}
